==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term/t|roa-opt|acordar}}, from {{etyl|VL.|pt}} {{term/t|la|*accordāre}}, present active infinitive of {{term/t|la|*accordō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/ɐ.kuɾ.ˈðaɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|a|cor|dar|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|acord|ar}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=pt}} to [[awake]] {{gloss|to gain consciousness}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[wake up]] {{gloss|a person, an animal, etc.}}
#*{{RQ:Harry Potter|3|pt-BR|page=336}}
#*: Francamente, vão '''acordar''' todo mundo!
#*:: Frankly, you are going to wake up everybody!

====Conjugation====
{{pt-conj|acord|ar}}

----

==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|VL.|es}} {{term/t|la|*accordare}}, from {{term/t|la|ac-}} (combining form of {{term/t|la|ad||to}}) +  {{term/t|la|cor||heart}}, + verb suffix {{term/t|la|-āre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/akoɾˈdaɾ/|lang=es}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|acord|ar|pres=acuerdo}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=es}} to [[decide]], [[arrange]]
# {{context|intransitive|lang=es}} to [[agree]]
#: {{usex|Lo '''acordaron''' por unanimidad.|t=They agreed to it unanimously.|inline=1|lang=es}}
# {{context|reflexive|[[acordarse]] de|lang=es}} to reach agreement
# {{context|reflexive|[[acordarse]] de|lang=es}} to [[remember]], [[recall]]
#: {{usex|¿'''Se acuerda''' Ud. '''de''' esto?|t=Do you remember this?|inline=1|lang=es}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|remember}} [[recordar]]

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj-ar (o-ue)|ac|rd}}

====Related terms====
* [[acordarse]]
* [[acorde]]
* [[acuerdo]]

